cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "m2metric: M2 (second spectral moment) as a downstream-aware verification metric for derivative-based diagnostics"
abstract: >-
  Data assimilation systems have been validated by RMSE (the zeroth spectral
  moment M0 of the background-error spectrum) for half a century. We show that
  any downstream diagnostic built on spatial derivatives has error dominated by
  the second spectral moment M2 = ∫k²E(k)dk, because the derivative operator is
  a high-pass filter in wavenumber space. This yields a systematic "metric
  blindness": RMSE misreports the value of scale-separation operators (which
  only reduce M2, not M0). We provide an analytic theorem (M2/M0 = k₀²/2 for a
  Gaussian spectrum), a four-to-six-fold amplification of derivative errors
  verified on independent radiosonde and COSMIC-2 GNSS radio-occultation
  observations, and a sufficient condition for scale-separation operators to be
  safe for derivative diagnostics (ringing-free + direction-preserving).
keywords:
  - data assimilation
  - verification metrics
  - error spectra
  - derivative diagnostics
  - turbulence
  - clear-air turbulence
  - aviation meteorology
license: MIT
